# Repository Guidelines

## Project Structure & Module Organization

Next.js 14 App Router project with two route groups under `src/app/`:
- **`(public)`** — customer-facing pages: tour catalog, booking, checkout, boarding pass, voucher, destinations, and info pages (about, faq, support, privacy, etc.)
- **`(admin)`** — admin dashboard: login, bookings, tours, destinations, reviews, notifications, campaigns, operations calendar, analytics, settings
- **`api/`** — API routes under `api/admin/`, `api/bookings/`, `api/checkout/`, `api/payments/`, `api/media/`, `api/auth/`, `api/notifications/`, `api/public/`

The `src/` directory separates components by domain:
- `components/admin/` — admin panel widgets (TourBuilderForm, MediaManager, AnalyticsDashboard, etc.)
- `components/landing/` — homepage sections (Hero, TourCatalog, PopularDestinations, FAQSection)
- `components/tours/` — booking flow widgets (BookingWidget, BookingFormSteps, TourTimeline)
- `components/checkout/` — checkout sidebar
- `components/public/` — shared public components (TourCard, TourGrid, ReviewSection)
- `components/ui/` — generic UI primitives (Button, RouteLoader, CarouselImages)
- `components/layout/` — layout wrappers
- `components/modals/` — modal overlays
- `components/vouchers/` — QR generator

Supabase handles authentication (magic link) and media storage (signed upload URLs). The client is initialized in `src/lib/supabase/client.ts`.

Internationalization uses hand-written locale files in `src/locales/` (en, de, es, fr, it, pl, ru). The Prisma schema stores multilingual content in JSON `translations` fields on Tour and Destination.

## Build, Test, and Development Commands

- `npm run dev` — start Next.js dev server
- `npm run build` — production build (`next build`)
- `npm run start` — start production server
- `npm run lint` — lint with `next lint` (no ESLint config file — relies on Next.js defaults)
- `npm run db:generate` — regenerate Prisma client
- `npm run db:push` — push schema to database
- `npm run db:studio` — open Prisma Studio

No test framework is configured.

## Coding Style & Naming Conventions

- TypeScript with `strict: true` and `@/*` path alias mapped to `./src/*`
- Tailwind CSS for styling (no CSS modules or styled-components)
- Lucide React icons used throughout
- Folder structure uses kebab-case for multi-word directories
- React components use PascalCase filenames; utilities use camelCase
- Server components by default; `'use client'` added only when interactivity is needed
- Prisma schema follows `@@map` convention for model-to-table name mapping

## Commit & Pull Request Guidelines

Conventional commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `merge:`, `@ <message>` prefixes seen in history. Keep commits focused on single concerns. No PR template detected.
